label chapter_4_chapter_i__down_the_rabbit_hole:
    # Chapter 4: CHAPTER I. Down the Rabbit-Hole

    # Scene setup
    # scene bg chapter_i__down_the_rabbit_hole with fade  # Use this if environment image exists
    scene bg default with fade
    # play music "audio/bgm.mp3" fadein 2.0  # Add music here

    # Scene description
    "The chapter begins on a riverbank on a hot summer day, where Alice sits beside her sister in drowsy boredom. The setting shifts dramatically when Alice follows the White Rabbit down a rabbit-hole beneath a hedge, which transforms into a tunnel before plunging into a very deep well. The well's sides are lined with cupboards, bookshelves, maps, and pictures hung on pegs, creating a surreal domestic quality to the vertical shaft. The fall seems endless, moving through darkness."

    "Alice eventually lands on a heap of sticks and dry leaves, emerging into a long, dark passage. She then enters a long, low hall illuminated by a row of lamps hanging from the roof, with doors locked all around its perimeter. Behind a low curtain, she discovers a tiny door opening onto a passage leading to a lovely garden with bright flower beds and cool fountains visible beyond—a sharp contrast to the dark, confined hall."


    # Character introductions
    show alice neutral at center with dissolve
    "A young girl, likely around seven to ten years old, with a curious"
    "and imaginative mind."

    show alice_s_sister neutral at center with dissolve
    "An older sibling present only at the opening, reading a book without"
    "pictures or conversations."

    show white_rabbit neutral at center with dissolve
    "An anthropomorphic rabbit with pink eyes, dressed in a waistcoat with"
    "a pocket containing a watch."

    # End of chapter
    scene black with fade
    "To be continued..."
    return
